{"id":"libretti-thamoskoniginagypten","title":"Thamos, König in Ägypten","composer":"Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart","language":"English","form":null,"source":"opera-guide.ch","source_url":"https://opera-guide.ch/operas/thamos+konig+in+agypten/libretto/en/","acts":[{"heading":"Act","scenes":[{"title":"","description":"","lines":[["","No. 1 - Chorus","dir"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","The night, day's enemy, gives place to you, o Sun!","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","From Egypt a fresh victim is offered to you:","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","hear our prayer! May your eternal course","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","bring happy days to the people of Thamos!","sung"],["PRIESTS","Grant to the happy youth of our land","sung"],["PRIESTS","the gifts of obedience and purity.","sung"],["PRIESTS","To the young men courage,","sung"],["PRIESTS","bravery in deed,","sung"],["PRIESTS","wisdom in counsel,","sung"],["PRIESTS","and to all grant love of their country!","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","Hear our prayer! May your eternal course","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","bring happy days to the people of Thamos!","sung"],["VIRGINS","May Egypt's daughters be","sung"],["VIRGINS","their families' and","sung"],["VIRGINS","their husbands' pride!","sung"],["VIRGINS","In quiet happiness","sung"],["VIRGINS","dutifully to live,","sung"],["VIRGINS","bloorning and full of years as we!","sung"],["PRIESTS","Crowned with victory","sung"],["PRIESTS","may Thamos in war","sung"],["PRIESTS","strike terror into our enemies!","sung"],["VIRGINS","Lead us through trials,","sung"],["VIRGINS","and tribulations, and through love,","sung"],["VIRGINS","o king and father!","sung"],["VIRGINS","Nr. 2 - Interlude (Maestoso - Allegro)","sung"],["","after Act One","dir"],["VIRGINS","Nr. 3 - Interlude (Andante)","sung"],["","after Act Two","dir"],["VIRGINS","Nr. 4 - Interlude (Allegro)","sung"],["","after Act Three","dir"],["VIRGINS","Nr. 5 - Interlude ( Allegro vivace assai)","sung"],["","after Act Four","dir"],["","No. 6 - Chorus","dir"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","Godhead mighty above all!","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","Ever renewed and ever glorious!","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","The land of Egypt worships you.","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","Ever rising, never falling,","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","let it be supreme o'er all,","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","in greatness knowing no equal!","sung"],["PRIESTS","From the hot sands of midday","sung"],["PRIESTS","to the distant ocean's edge","sung"],["PRIESTS","clouds of incense rise.","sung"],["PRIESTS","Early on our songs are heard,","sung"],["PRIESTS","each evening once again our hymns;","sung"],["PRIESTS","never does our chorus remain silent.","sung"],["VIRGINS","As in the vasty temple's halls","sung"],["VIRGINS","with the trumpet's blast","sung"],["VIRGINS","blends the soft enchanted flute,","sung"],["VIRGINS","so blends, o sons of Osiris,","sung"],["VIRGINS","our song with yours","sung"],["VIRGINS","a song of praise to you, o sun!","sung"],["A PRIEST","What the prince's words promise,","sung"],["A VIRGIN","What the people ask of him,","sung"],["BOTH","May each bring blessing down on each!","sung"],["A PRIEST","He gracious to us,","sung"],["A VIRGIN","We faithful to the throne;","sung"],["A PRIEST","Fatherly care,","sung"],["A VIRGIN","Our love in return,","sung"],["BOTH","That is our mutual bond.","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","Godhead rnighty above all!","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","Ever renewed and ever glorious!","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","The land of Egypt worships you.","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","Ever rising, never falling,","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","let it be supreme o'er all,","sung"],["PRIESTS, VIRGINS","in greatness knowing no equal!","sung"],["","Nr. 7 a - Interlude","dir"],["","after Act Five","dir"],["","No. 7b - Solo and Chorus","dir"],["HIGH PRIEST","Ye children of the dust, tremble and quake","sung"],["HIGH PRIEST","e'er ye rise up against the god!","sung"],["HIGH PRIEST","Avenging thunderbolts protect him","sung"],["HIGH PRIEST","from the blasphemer's vain attack!","sung"],["CHORUS","We children of the dust tremble and quake,","sung"],["CHORUS","and bow our heads to the earth;","sung"],["CHORUS","to serve the gods be our sole endeavour,","sung"],["CHORUS","in whatsoever they desire.","sung"],["CHORUS","Mightiest godhead, gentle Sun,","sung"],["CHORUS","hear Egypt's pious prayer!","sung"],["CHORUS","Protect the king's new crown,","sung"],["CHORUS","let it never fall.","sung"]]}]}]}